{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae","id":261432,"title":"Space Opera Changeling & Cosmic True Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-20T13:05:26-07:00","id":261432,"title":"Space Opera Changeling & Cosmic True Fae","content":"Does anyone else feel like Guardians of the Galaxy is like a Changeling the Lost game set in space? Well, minus the contracts and Hedge. Love 'em both, too. You got your beast, your elemental, an ogre, a gadgety wizened (Starlord?) and Green-skinned Fairest. <i>Beautiful. </i>But getting to the point, could you potentially use the setting of GotG as inspiration for how Changeling would work in a sci-fi space opera?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T13:18:46-07:00","id":264079,"title":"","content":"Hmm... What if freeholds were more akin to starships? Or perhaps a new type in addition to ones that are based planet-side? If designed as such, perhaps a court system based around aspects of space travel would be possible? CtL becomes Changeling, the Lost in Space! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Additionally, given how out of place organic plant matter would be inside a vacuum, what if the void of the Hedge became sort of like a place of infinite possibility? Given how the Hedge is all about enchantment and madness, we apply that to Mankind's imagination when pertaining to space flight. That is, our dreams of traveling the stars become the elements in which we base the &quot;Expanse&quot; or &quot;Nebula&quot;? (Or whatever you wanna call it).<br /> <br /> To avoid alienating (no pun intended) players of normal Changeling from the setting, we keep the seasons. However, since there's no real sense of time in space, a freehold is divided into 4 branches, each season's leader representing the top, who act as the admirals of a freehold fleet and/or ship. To prevent tyrannical oppression from one season's monopoly, each is allowed personal military units, medical staff, and engineers. However, the only way to confuse the True Fae is to ensure people share power. Thus, only one season can command a section of the ship and its units, unless vetoed by the other three.<br /> <br /> Example: Only the Summer Court can command a ship's weapons battery and munitions, but if needed, the other court leaders may veto his/her say if it threatens the freehold's safety.<br /> <br /> Spring -- Diplomacy, Medicine, Morale<br /> Summer -- Defense, Security, War<br /> Autumn -- Logistics, Science/Engineering, R&amp;D<br /> Winter -- Communication, Navigation, Recon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T15:08:27-07:00","id":264158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae?p=264079#post264079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, given how out of place organic plant matter would be inside a vacuum, what if the void of the Hedge became sort of like a place of infinite possibility? Given how the Hedge is all about enchantment and madness, we apply that to Mankind's imagination when pertaining to space flight. That is, our dreams of traveling the stars become the elements in which we base the &quot;Expanse&quot; or &quot;Nebula&quot;? (Or whatever you wanna call it).</div> </div> </div> </div>*straight face*<br /> <br /> The Warp?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T15:11:44-07:00","id":264161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae?p=264158#post264158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*straight face*<br /> <br /> The Warp?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wanna go that route, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T15:51:42-07:00","id":264204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae?p=264161#post264161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanna go that route, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, the Warp's too sane; it only wants to kill you and obeys no internal logic.<br /> <br /> Depending on what clauses you've triggered in the Hedge, it may create a true oasis for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T16:08:29-07:00","id":264220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae?p=264204#post264204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, the Warp's too sane; it only wants to kill you and obeys no internal logic.<br /> <br /> Depending on what clauses you've triggered in the Hedge, it may create a true oasis for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. But the use of &quot;Hedge&quot; connotes vegetation of some kind. Though not always the case (especially in urban reflections), Hedge gives off the wrong idea. Said-urban environment was called &quot;The City&quot; in Autumn Horrors, while in others its called &quot;The Jungle&quot; or &quot;The Woods&quot;. What would be a good name to give the void-space of the Hedge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T16:47:34-07:00","id":264262,"title":"","content":"The Galactic Leyline? :3<br /> <br /> The Expanse works. Random other suggestions: The Reaches, The Frontier, The Infinity, The Beyond, The Continuum, and The Brink. ... <span style=\"font-size:9px\">And The 'verse.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T22:12:22-07:00","id":264389,"title":"","content":"There is a supplement that mentions the WoD in space, including the Hedge. Take a look at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T08:50:30-07:00","id":264630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae?p=264389#post264389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a supplement that mentions the WoD in space, including the Hedge. Take a look at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did. Felt it could use some work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T14:40:18-07:00","id":264895,"title":"","content":"Ego, The Living Planet could be seen as a more blatant manifestation of a True Fae as both Actor and Realm. (Same goes for Mogo of the Green Lanterns or perhaps Danny the Street, though I believe Ego predates both.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T15:16:40-07:00","id":264910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae?p=264895#post264895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ego, The Living Planet could be seen as a more blatant manifestation of a True Fae as both Actor and Realm. (Same goes for Mogo of the Green Lanterns or perhaps Danny the Street, though I believe Ego predates both.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Either that or the biggest Hobgoblin ever conceived. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T16:05:09-07:00","id":264968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae?p=264262#post264262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Galactic Leyline? :3<br /> <br /> The Expanse works. Random other suggestions: The Reaches, The Frontier, The Infinity, The Beyond, The Continuum, and The Brink. ... <span style=\"font-size:9px\">And The 'verse.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of Arcadia as &quot;The Black&quot; from Firefly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T17:33:05-07:00","id":266524,"title":"","content":"I thought as a Changeling fan and one of space-faring scifi that I'd add to this... I see the Hedge in a space-based game being like some dark warp-space ala Event Horizon, but also I think it could work as a concept pretty much unchanged in a vein similar to Pandorum... That an element of the crew of a ship when in stasis or grav-couches (depending on how hard you want your scifi) and in the sustained coma dream-state are snatched from their dreams by the True Fae. Or perhaps they get snagged up as a side-effect of warp travel opens smaller portals inside the ship to The Hedge.<br /> I like the element of not everyone on a ship being a Changeling, that the Freehold is something that exists on the ship as it does in a city, for the Lost to pool together and get support. I've yet to think about how Fetches could be incorporated into the setting... I'm thinking of a setting where the actual warp-drive is a nebulous device that can open up portals in the ship to the Hedge and thus the Fae can come in, snag a crewman and replace them with a Fetch...<br /> <br /> Opinions? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T19:08:01-07:00","id":266561,"title":"","content":"I somehow picture the Seasonal Courts (as well as Day, Night, Dawn and Dusk) being more prominent in Freeholds settled on actual planets and moons, while the Directional Court system is more often adopted by spacefaring Freeholds. Does that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T09:14:50-07:00","id":266784,"title":"","content":"I would say I'd probably change the Directional Court names to the Traveller parlance, as in space North, South, East and West are pretty meaningless. Instead it would be more sensible to see the Directional Courts as in relation to moving in relation to the galaxy... So they would be Coreward, Rimward, Trailing and Spinward respectively <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I think as crew on a ship, the Courts would need some work tbh. In general there are supervisors in a crew and there could be a power struggle between a Lost crewmember following the orders of their Court's Crown and someone who is not Lost but higher up the foodchain so to speak. Of course this could happen in a general Lost game if some Lost happened to work in a place together where their supervisor or boss was not Lost themselves. It does bring another facet to 'mortal life' and 'fae life' needing to be balanced which is an inherent part of life as a Lost...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T02:23:34-07:00","id":268105,"title":"","content":"Well for what the walls of the hedge would manifest like in space, I'd go with an asteroid field, the path would be the path through the asteroids....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T04:49:11-07:00","id":268169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae?p=268105#post268105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well for what the walls of the hedge would manifest like in space, I'd go with an asteroid field, the path would be the path through the asteroids....</div> </div> </div> </div>Han Solo: &quot;Never tell me the odds.&quot; &gt;B3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T10:58:27-07:00","id":268350,"title":"","content":"Mr.Space Science-Me comes in now by saying that an Asteroid Field IRL are generally quite widely spaced out... Its near impossible to have problems navigating them when they're miles and miles apart... Space you see is incredibly, incredibly big... But seeing as we're dealing with Fae magicks and FTL is likely a thing with an Event-Horizon style drive... I think we can say that the Hedge acting as a tunnel of tightly packed asteroids when you get in there is fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Personally, I'd have had the Hedge act as some kind of warped spaceship corridor if it opens within the ship for the Gentry to snatch crew... Again calling up Event Horizon or perhaps Dead Space to make the Hedge suitably creepy... If we're talking a ship taken whole-sale... I'd make it like a wormhole similar to the 40K Warp within...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T16:12:29-07:00","id":273300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae?p=268350#post268350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mr.Space Science-Me comes in now by saying that an Asteroid Field IRL are generally quite widely spaced out... Its near impossible to have problems navigating them when they're miles and miles apart... Space you see is incredibly, incredibly big... But seeing as we're dealing with Fae magicks and FTL is likely a thing with an Event-Horizon style drive... I think we can say that the Hedge acting as a tunnel of tightly packed asteroids when you get in there is fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Personally, I'd have had the Hedge act as some kind of warped spaceship corridor if it opens within the ship for the Gentry to snatch crew... Again calling up Event Horizon or perhaps Dead Space to make the Hedge suitably creepy... If we're talking a ship taken whole-sale... I'd make it like a wormhole similar to the 40K Warp within...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's potential in this one...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T17:22:30-07:00","id":273334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae#post261432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else feel like Guardians of the Galaxy is like a Changeling the Lost game set in space? Well, minus the contracts and Hedge. Love 'em both, too. You got your beast, your elemental, an ogre, a gadgety wizened (Starlord?) and Green-skinned Fairest. <i>Beautiful. </i>But getting to the point, could you potentially use the setting of GotG as inspiration for how Changeling would work in a sci-fi space opera?</div> </div> </div> </div>o god no...<br /> <br /> This is more like Changeling in space:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://litreactor.com/sites/default/files/images/column/2013/11/keltiad.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>....<br /> <br /> <i>... posits a universe where Celts took to the stars ahead of the other people of Earth, establishing the interstellar kingdom of Keltia. The series draws on Celtic and pagan cultural ideas, pairing them with advanced technologies that exist alongside magic. Later books in the series went on to draw on Arthurian myth and legend.</i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T05:03:46-07:00","id":273623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nah, the Warp's too sane; it only wants to kill you and obeys no internal logic. </div> </div> </div>Unless you verge into domains into one of Chaos Gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And then Slaanesh is just looking at all this with interest, his eyes narrowed, and he says; &quot;hmm, that's an interesting act, what do you call yourselves?&quot; and True Fae stick their chests out and go; &quot;The Aristocrats!&quot; </div> </div> </div>More seriously, I plan for interstellar setting for NWoD, and I assumed aside from more arduous but safer subluminar travel voidships can go through the Underworld, Twilight and Hedge depending on the type of FTL engine, with necessary protections. Suddenly a Sin-Eater, Urathra or Changeling becomes a valuable member of the crew like 40K's Navigators.<br /> <br /> And Freebooters are reavers that raid colonies of humans and homeworlds of aliens alike to sell slaves at the Goblin Market. I already figured out that some remnants of Lancea Et Sanctum (Covenant system crumbled due to humans discovering existence of Vampires and the latter having to redefine their social structure) taken up raiding colonies of humans in emulation of L&amp;S goal to scare humans straight into righteous behavior and employing Night Lords' tactics. Hence, with addition of Power Armor they are unholy mix of Blood Angels, Word Bearers and Night Lord. They also carved out small system wide on the borders of the interstellar state of humans to maintain secure flow of blood, ghouls and Embrace candidates. Locals are scared into submission, but at the same time Kindred protect their herd from some nastier threats. Including bands of Freebooters.<br /> <br /> The fleet of the human state would crush Freebooters, Kindred Reavers and other assorted pirate scum if it could focus its full might on one task. Instead, the navy wages small scare wars and skirmishes with varied results, and while bulk of void farers are mortals, there are supernatural experts hired in exchange for protection. Even Vampires, whose particular needs are glossed over as long as they are loyal in their service. Particularly trustworthy ones can even Embrace though the candidate must be approved by their superiors. <br /> <br /> But I'm going off tangent, needless to say. I need to figure out how Changelings can fit into such setting so I appreciate the thread's creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-06-2014, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T12:13:34-07:00","id":274084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae?p=264968#post264968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Arcadia as &quot;The Black&quot; from Firefly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, re-reading this, it works a lot better than I initially thought: what if Changelings are Reavers who have regained the capacity for civilization? They have to hide what they once were, and they never really lose the abyss yawning inside them (that would be Promethean's shtick), but they're struggling to fit back into civilized society again, even if it's the frontier.<br /> <br /> It's a lot more one-dimensional than C:tL (how many types of Reavers are there, really?), but it retains its quintessence in a sci-fi setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T13:03:20-07:00","id":274123,"title":"","content":"&quot;Dreams and nightmares connect the stars faster than ships. Even through the void, you cannot escape them.&quot;<br /> <br /> This quote provided by my pal Yolf as his response to the idea of using Hedge as FTL passage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T13:19:34-07:00","id":274130,"title":"","content":"When I think of a true fae in space, the first thing that springs to mind is Fletcher Hanks' creation: 'Stardust, the Space Wizard'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T23:25:47-07:00","id":277022,"title":"","content":"Having just railed through Babylon 5, you could honestly look at the war between the Vorlons and Shadows as a Fey game. They're only trying to convince others they're right, but they frame it as this epic war between light and dark, good and evil, when really it's about obliterating the opposing viewpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4042-chessvice","name":"ChessVice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T12:36:53-07:00","id":277495,"title":"","content":"BTW, what about alien Changelings? If I make Hedge reach worlds beyond Solar System, then an alien race could be taken by True Fae doing weird things on them for their own amusement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T17:14:22-07:00","id":277692,"title":"","content":"Katsura, what is that quote from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T17:24:37-07:00","id":277694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w9LE5TNomvc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w9LE5TNomvc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w9LE5TNomvc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w9LE5TNomvc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This song.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T20:21:12-07:00","id":277795,"title":"","content":"Thanks you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:28:53-07:00","id":281230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae?p=274084#post274084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, re-reading this, it works a lot better than I initially thought: what if Changelings are Reavers who have regained the capacity for civilization? They have to hide what they once were, and they never really lose the abyss yawning inside them (that would be Promethean's shtick), but they're struggling to fit back into civilized society again, even if it's the frontier.<br /> <br /> It's a lot more one-dimensional than C:tL (how many types of Reavers are there, really?), but it retains its quintessence in a sci-fi setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;We didn't <i>mean</i> to, OK? We just wanted this to be a better world. And with all those bloodsuckers and monsters running around, we thought... we thought we needed a leg up.&quot;<br /> <br /> *Pause. The speaker sips his beer. He seems to collect his nerve, and continues.*<br /> <br /> &quot;We found it on a forest moon somewhere out in the Far Arm; no, I won't tell you where. It was a little plant that had some kind of natural nanotech - it gets in your system, and suddenly you can manipulate torsion fields or some shit. I dunno, I was just administration.<br /> <br /> The brains in R&amp;D thought they were so clever, too, reverse engineering it - it was a fucking <i>instruction manual</i>. They figured out how the plant did it, made a geneline treatment and everything. Fuckers missed what prolonged exposure to this stuff did to your noggin; apparently it just eats up the parts of the brain that handle empathy right up. You know how we found out?<br /> <br /> Some clumsy fucker, some dumbass <i>dropped a beaker.</i> Everyone on the station got infected, and - well, you've seen the footage.<br /> <br /> Me? No, I wasn't on the station. I was on vacation at the time; thank gods for small favors. Well, I'll be seeing you around.&quot;<br /> <br /> *The speaker finishes his beer and gets up to leave; as he passes under the lights, you could swear his shadow was too big. And he's a little short to have to stoop when going through the door.*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:43:06-07:00","id":281259,"title":"","content":"I actually figured out how to go through Hedge for Voidships.<br /> <br /> 1) Have a Demon associate who can build sufficiently powerful Rip Gate imbued Gadget.<br /> <br /> 2) Hire and/or befriend Changeling pal who will navigate through Hedge and open Hedge gate to the Fallen World<br /> <br /> 3) Now you can run Star Trek like space opera with Demon and Changeling as your token non-mortal members of the crew. Time to screw up plans of both Gentry and God-Machine while knocking up hot space ladies.<br /> <br /> Realtalk, for my ported non-Mage Technocracy's Void Engineers it will be imperative to be in good standing with Changelings and Demons, especially if their goal to protect everyone from alien and extradimensional threats will stay. No way they shall stay idle witnessing how Angels and Gentry meddle in human affairs. Intersplat bromance* awaits. <br /> <br /> *sismance and regular romance fine too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-14-2014, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T07:05:02-07:00","id":282237,"title":"","content":"OK, here's a thought.<br /> <br /> The Hedge looks like a version of the real world, distorted into hedge-y forms - in the country it looks like bramble-overgrown paths, at sea it looks seaweed-choked and filled with rocks, in the city it looks ... like various things, but a parklike version and weed-choked, ruined building show up. This woks the other way as well - the Hedge outside a frozen tundra Realm of Arcadia is snow-covered conifer, etc.<br /> <br /> So ... there's not a lot of scenery in space. It's basically just stars, planets and galaxies - dots moving in different patterns. Maybe the odd nebula or asteroid field, but those are localized (and much more &quot;spread out&quot; than they look.)<br /> <br /> What if in the Hedge around a location in outer space - whether somebody's space-themed Durance or a starship being moved by a hyperdrive Token - the stars stretch and distort into strands of, well, <i>hedge</i> forming walls around whatever path you're following? A la <i>Star Trek</i> or <i>Star Wars</i> FTL drives? Of course, without shields the hyper-accelerated particles will tear you and your ship to pieces.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, there's no Twilight, Shadow or Underworld in the Hedge/Arcadia, right? Spirits, Ghosts etc can still <i>exist</i> there, but they're material? That might have an interesting impact on how different splats behave on a starship.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/261432-space-opera-changeling-cosmic-true-fae?p=281259#post281259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually figured out how to go through Hedge for Voidships.<br /> <br /> 1) Have a Demon associate who can build sufficiently powerful Rip Gate imbued Gadget.<br /> <br /> 2) Hire and/or befriend Changeling pal who will navigate through Hedge and open Hedge gate to the Fallen World<br /> <br /> 3) Now you can run Star Trek like space opera with Demon and Changeling as your token non-mortal members of the crew. Time to screw up plans of both Gentry and God-Machine while knocking up hot space ladies.<br /> <br /> Realtalk, for my ported non-Mage Technocracy's Void Engineers it will be imperative to be in good standing with Changelings and Demons, especially if their goal to protect everyone from alien and extradimensional threats will stay. No way they shall stay idle witnessing how Angels and Gentry meddle in human affairs. Intersplat bromance* awaits.<br /> <br /> *sismance and regular romance fine too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, would they be a hunter Conspiracy, then?<br /> <br /> [Wait, does Rip Gate work on the Hedge? Is that a thing? I could have sworn it was Underworld and Shadow only... awesome, if so.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T07:12:21-07:00","id":282261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Huh, would they be a hunter Conspiracy, then? </div> </div> </div>Mechanics wise, surely, I need just to figure proper Endowments and Status bonuses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 The Hedge: The barrier between the mortal world and Arcadia, the strange home of the Fair Folk. Most humans<br /> only see the Hedge if they are being dragged through it to be enslaved by the Fae, and it is a decidedly unpredictable<br /> place. The biggest challenge for demons is that once they have entered the Hedge, they can\u2019t use Rip the Gates to<br /> get out again. Changelings and other denizens can sometimes open gateways back to Earth, but they might demand<br /> bargains or services and some of them are just as shrewd at making pacts as any demon. </div> </div> </div>Rip The Gates can be used to reach The Hedge, just you cannot come out without help of a Changeling that can open a gateway back.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I found this unfinished tidbit and 1d4chan and I'm quite intrigued:<br /> <b>Court of Iron</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>The mind is a machine. Or the product of a machine, the brain. You know this to be true. What you and I experienced was nothing more nor less than a protracted malfunction. There is a process to fix things. It may seem... fanciful, at first, but I assure you, it's temporary. Soon, we can put all fantasy behind us. Which will you trust: The false ephemera of dreams, or cold, solid Iron?</i></span></span></span><ul><li>Emotion - Closure</li> <li>Associations - Banality, order, stability, reality, guns, metal, gray, community, swords, technology, humanity, normalcy, mundanity, solidarity, denial.</li> <li>Contracts of Crystalization - Forcing a fixed form on ideas, concepts, and eventually reality. Shutting down Hedge gates.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-15-2014, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank"